			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1900601">
									

<p>I gotta say, this somehow reminded me of the movie The Day the Earth Stood Still, with the cylinder and the hostile insect (which have reminded me of Kha'Zix from LoL). About the procedure 2000 Filigree and the problems with 2000's containment, am I at least partially right with the thought that they fill the gaps with some kind of a liquid sealing matter? Like clay, but of course more durable?</p>
<p>I also wondered about the bond 2000 had with Dr. Clark, which was elaborated upon in the last interview.</p>
<p>This is a very psychological, &quot;character-driven&quot;, if you want, piece and provokes many thoughts. Whether 2000 was a liar or not, whether he is continuing his deception through 2000-1, or if he is actually right and his &quot;people&quot; want to help us&#8230; it asks many questions for the reader to answer. For me, &lt;headcanon&gt; 2000-1 was lying about the help as much as you can imagine &lt;/headcanon&gt;</p>
<p>This is a first psychological take on 2000 I have seen here and for the execution, I award it with +1. Dunno if it should make 2000, it's certainly not bad, but very one-sided. So, no opinion on that. Good job!</p>

